        {
          "id": 1918246134,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Ayyyy, I gather this code will only get built in \"real\" Windows builds -- the Fedora MinGW merge pipeline build succeeded but WSDG explains that that doesn't include airpcap, so extra caution was required there.  Sorry for the breakage!\n\nIn the last few days, I have managed to break the Falco bridge (e60926f8), Debian packaging (c0100f57) and now Windows ws80211_utils, all from adding a new header.  If I keep going at this rate, it might start looking like I am _trying_ to break things! :disappointed:\n\nAgain, my apologies.\n\nThe fix looks good to me.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7889756,
            "username": "dariusd0",
